FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/01_journals/Dailies/2026-04-07.md
---
alias: []
created: 2025-10-18T13:25:33+00:00
journal: Daily
journal-date: 2026-04-07
modified: 2026-04-09T08:11:13+00:00
title: 2026-04-07
type: daily
updated:
---
---

- Thinking about knowledge. If I want a personal knowledge management system I should define what knowledge is.
   - THis is important. With LLM giving us the kind of search that looks intelligent it is changing what I think knowledge and intelligence is. I don't think that what llm does is intelligent. I don't like even calling it AI. But if it isn't intelligence then what is?
- what differentiates personal knowledge from other knowledge? Can knowledge be claimed?
- I have a new feeling about the ai slop. Now I am thinking about what knowledge is I resist asking AI because it will churn out a convincing block of text but I no longer trust that.
- if I can reliably ask LLM for the answer there is little need for PKM.
- personal opinion management
- personal certainty management
- personal understanding management
CONTENT_START:

```journal-nav

```

