FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Timeboxing is Allocating Specific Time Slots for Specific Tasks.md
---
aliases: ["Timeboxing Definition"]
created: 2025-11-01T21:00:00Z
last_reviewed: "2025-11-01"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:24+00:00
status: "evergreen"
tags: ["definition", "scheduling", "time-management", "topic/productivity"]
title: Timeboxing is Allocating Specific Time Slots for Specific Tasks
type: "concept"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Timeboxing is the practice of dedicating specific, fixed blocks of time to particular tasks or activities.

Unlike an open-ended to-do list where tasks are listed without a schedule, timeboxing assigns each task a concrete allocation on a calendar. This transforms a vague intention into a specific commitment.

