FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Coherent LLM output signals meaningful processing.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-10-20T09:17:00Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:35+00:00
status: ""
tags: ["coherence", "SoftwareEngineering/AI", "TheHuman/Cognition"]
title: Coherent LLM output signals meaningful processing
type: ""
updated: 
---
---

Links: [[LLMs mimic human conversational patterns]]
CONTENT_START:

A key part of LLM-driven validation comes from the coherence and logical structure of its responses. When we express a complex idea, we might anticipate a confused or meaningless reply from a non-understanding entity.

An LLM provides the opposite: a structured, coherent analysis that breaks down ideas and draws connections. This coherence signals to us that our thoughts have been processed in a meaningful way, even if that processing is purely algorithmic. This subversion of our negative expectations reinforces the perceived merit of our original thoughts.

---
