FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Mathematical Constants as Fundamental Ratios and Processes.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-08-30T08:59:02Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:31+00:00
status: ""
tags: ["constants", "TheHuman/Cognition/mental-model", "topic/maths"]
title: Mathematical Constants as Fundamental Ratios and Processes
type: ""
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Many important numbers are not quantities for counting but are concepts representing fundamental relationships or processes in the universe.

- Pi ($\pi$): Is not just the string of digits $3.14159…$ It _is_ the perfect, unchanging ratio of any circle's circumference to its diameter. It's a fundamental constant of geometry.
- Euler's Number ($e$): Represents the concept of perfect, continuous growth. It is the base rate of change found throughout nature and finance.
