title: Motion Creates Emotion to Overcome Inertia
type: "hypothesis"
updated: 
---
---

## 2. Experiment Protocol

- Duration: 3 Days.
- Trigger: Whenever I catch myself sitting and "waiting to feel like it" or saying "I'm just not motivated."
- Action:

    1. Identify: Pick one "stupidly small" physical movement (e.g., stand up, put on shoes, touch the dish sponge).
CONTENT_START:

## 1. The Hypothesis

> If I force a physical action _before_ I feel the emotional desire or "motivation" to act,
> Then the feeling of motivation will genuinely follow the action,
