FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Evil Attacks the Shared Moral Community Itself Not Merely a Norm Within It.md
---
created: 2026-04-10T13:00:00+00:00
modified: 2026-04-10T16:52:03+00:00
tags: [community, morality, social-order, sociology]
title: Evil Attacks the Shared Moral Community Itself Not Merely a Norm Within It
---
CONTENT_START:

## Evil Attacks the Shared Moral Community Itself Not Merely a Norm Within It

Ordinary wrongdoing violates particular norms _within_ a shared moral framework—it is a transgression that the framework itself is designed to address. Evil differs by attacking the _framework itself_—the foundational assumption of common humanity and mutual recognition that makes moral community possible. This is why evil produces horror and not merely condemnation: it threatens the conditions under which moral response is possible at all.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Inaction Erodes Self-Trust.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-10-20T08:05:02Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:32+00:00
status: ""
tags: ["confidence", "inaction", "self_esteem", "TheHuman/Psychology"]
title: Inaction Erodes Self-Trust
type: ""
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

The continuous loop of learning but never doing, a key feature of [[The Intelligence Trap - Strategist vs Performer]] and a form of [[motion_vs_action|motion without action]], has a significant hidden cost: the erosion of trust and belief in oneself.

When you repeatedly fail to act on your own plans, you begin to form a negative [[Self-Esteem and Identity|identity]] of being "intelligent but useless." Each private failure reinforces this negative self-perception, leading to a further loss of confidence. This makes it even harder for the "Performer" to act in the future, creating a downward spiral of inaction and diminishing self-worth that closely resembles [[The Shame-Procrastination Cycle]]. This cycle is often exacerbated by [[ADHD Paralysis is the Inability to Start a Task Until it Becomes an Emergency|ADHD paralysis]] and can manifest as [[Productive Procrastination as an Avoidance Strategy]].

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Event-based pacing matches boom and bust energy cycles.md
---
aliases: ["Boom-bust pacing", "Energy cycle matching"]
created: 2025-10-30T17:36:00Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:34+00:00
source: "[[MOC - How To Create And Use Mini Routines]]"
status: "seedling"
tags: ["autism", "energy-management", "TheHuman/Health/ADHD"]
title: Event-based pacing matches boom and bust energy cycles
type: "concept"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Event-based pacing systems can match the natural "boom and bust" energy cycles common in ADHD and autism by allowing high-energy periods to run longer and low-energy periods to compress or rest, rather than forcing all activities into predetermined time blocks.

"Boom and bust" refers to the oscillating pattern where individuals experience periods of high capability and intense productivity followed by periods of depletion and reduced functioning. Time-based schedules often fail because they assume consistent energy availability throughout the day and week.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/LLM Context Constraints.md
---
type: atom
status: seed
kind: constraint
source_title: "AI Agent Architecture and the Modern Tech Stack"
source_url: "https://gemini.google.com/app/509937047bd0b955"
created_utc: "2026-04-13T11:20:00Z"
confidence: high
tags:
  - llm
  - context-window
  - memory
  - tokens
upstream: "[[HEAD You said Persona You are an expert research analy... 3]]"
---
CONTENT_START:

## LLM Context Constraints

Large Language Models are restricted by a finite token-based context window that serves as the model's immediate short-term memory. Because expanding this window increases both latency and operational cost, external memory solutions and efficient context management are required for long-term or data-intensive projects.

