FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Discreteness as a Precondition for Counting.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-08-30T08:59:28Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:34+00:00
status: ""
tags: ["foundations", "physics", "topic/maths", "topic/philosophy"]
title: Discreteness as a Precondition for Counting
type: ""
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

For the act of counting and the concept of number to be meaningful, the universe must contain distinction or discreteness. We must be able to perceive separate, distinct things.

Counting requires the ability to identify an object and distinguish it from its background and from other objects. It is the fundamental difference between what is discrete (countable, like apples) and what is continuous (an unbroken whole, like a flow of water).

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Dereflection Counters Rumination by Redirecting Attention from Self to External Values.md
---
created: 2026-04-10T00:00:00+00:00
modified: 2026-04-10T16:52:03+00:00
tags: [anxiety, attention, technique, therapy]
title: Dereflection Counters Rumination by Redirecting Attention from Self to External Values
---
CONTENT_START:

## Dereflection Counters Rumination by Redirecting Attention from Self to External Values

Dereflection is Frankl's logotherapeutic technique for breaking self-focused anxiety and hyper-reflection loops. Rather than trying to suppress anxious thoughts or analyse them further—both of which intensify the self-focus—the technique redirects attention outward toward an external goal, a person who needs help, or a value the individual is committed to. The loop is interrupted not by fighting it from within but by changing the direction of attention entirely.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Folgezettel Is Not Hierarchical.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2024-03-19T10:45:55Z
id: "1b1"
last_reviewed: "null"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:33+00:00
status: "null"
tags: ["note-taking", "topic/pkm/zettelkasten"]
title: Folgezettel Is Not Hierarchical
type: "permanent"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Folgezettel (the alphanumeric ID system) is often misinterpreted as creating a hierarchical tree structure. This is incorrect. While IDs like 1.1a1 appear to suggest that the note is a "child" of 1.1a, this is merely an addressing convention, not a parent-child relationship.

Example: Note 1.1a about "apples are healthy" and 1.1a1 about "the history of apple cultivation" are not in a hierarchical relationship - they simply share an address space that indicates they were created in sequence and are related.

---
