FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Continuous Autonomous Agent Loops Incur Significant API Cost.md
---
created: 2026-04-10T12:00:00+00:00
modified: 2026-04-10T16:52:03+00:00
tags: [api-costs, constraints, economics, scalability]
title: Continuous Autonomous Agent Loops Incur Significant API Cost
---
CONTENT_START:

## Continuous Autonomous Agent Loops Incur Significant API Cost

Continuous autonomous agent loops without human-in-the-loop intervention incur substantial operational cost: approximately $20 per agent per hour at commercial LLM API rates (2025 pricing). A single three-hour single-agent run costs ~$60; a multi-agent setup can exceed hundreds of dollars in a single day. This financial constraint is not an edge case—it is a primary architectural pressure on agentic system design.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Unpredictable Rewards Accelerate Habit Formation.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-10-30T12:05:09Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:24+00:00
source: "[[MOC - The Science of Making and Breaking Habits]]"
status: "seedling"
tags: ["dopamine", "rewards", "TheHuman/Habits", "TheHuman/Neuroscience"]
title: Unpredictable Rewards Accelerate Habit Formation
type: "concept"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Dopaminergic rewards accelerate habit formation, but unpredictable or "surprise" rewards have the strongest effect. The brain responds more strongly to unexpected positive outcomes. This principle can be leveraged by using subjective anticipation and self-reward, but avoiding consistently externalizing rewards, to increase the "stickiness" of a new habit.
