FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Phaedrus Adapted Aesop's Fables into Latin Verse.md
---
aliases: ["Phaedrus' Latin Fables"]
created: 2025-11-01T21:36:00Z
last_reviewed: "2025-11-01"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:29+00:00
status: "evergreen"
tags: ["fable", "history", "latin-literature", "phaedrus", "storytelling"]
title: "Phaedrus Adapted Aesop's Fables into Latin Verse"
type: "concept"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Phaedrus, a Roman poet of the 1st century CE, played a crucial role in the evolution of the fable by translating Aesop's oral tales into Latin verse.

This was a significant shift from oral to literary tradition. By composing the fables as poetry, Phaedrus elevated their status from simple folk tales to a recognized literary genre within the Roman world. His work was instrumental in preserving the Aesopic tradition and transmitting it through written culture, allowing the fables to be studied and read by educated audiences.
---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Routines reduce anxiety and decision fatigue in neurodivergent individuals.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-10-30T16:20:00Z
last_reviewed: "null"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:28+00:00
source: ""
status: "seedling"
tags: ["anxiety-reduction", "autism", "decision-fatigue", "TheHuman/Health/ADHD"]
title: Routines reduce anxiety and decision fatigue in neurodivergent individuals
type: "concept"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Routines significantly reduce anxiety, sensory overwhelm, and decision fatigue in autistic and ADHD individuals by minimizing the cognitive load required for daily functioning and providing predictable structure that reduces the need for constant decision-making.

Event-based mini routines offer a particularly effective approach by reducing time-pressure anxiety. Rather than being tied to specific clock times, these routines trigger from natural life events (like finishing a meal or completing a work block), which minimizes the stress of clock-watching and allows for natural adaptation to daily variations in energy, motivation, and unexpected circumstances.

---
