FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Bearer Tokens.md
---
type: atom
status: seed
kind: mechanism
source_title: "Every API Authentication Method Explained"
source_url: "https://youtube.com/watch?v=_lTECv25N2U"
created_utc: "2026-04-13T11:30:00Z"
confidence: high
tags:
  - security
  - authentication
  - bearer-tokens
  - stateless
upstream: "[[HEAD Authentication Methods and Concepts]]"
---
CONTENT_START:

## Bearer Tokens

Bearer Tokens grant access to any entity that possesses the token, eliminating the need for server-side session storage. This stateless approach is widely used in modern APIs but requires rigorous protection, such as short expiration times and transport encryption, to prevent impersonation if the token is stolen.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Meaning-Driven Activity Activates Brain Reward Systems Independently of External Reinforcement.md
---
created: 2026-04-10T00:00:00+00:00
modified: 2026-04-10T16:52:03+00:00
tags: [adhd, dopamine, motivation, neuroscience]
title: Meaning-Driven Activity Activates Brain Reward Systems Independently of External Reinforcement
---
CONTENT_START:

## Meaning-Driven Activity Activates Brain Reward Systems Independently of External Reinforcement

Purpose-driven activities engage brain regions involved in reward processing—the ventral tegmental area and nucleus accumbens—producing dopamine-mediated motivation without requiring an external reward. This creates a secondary reward pathway that operates independently of the typical external-reinforcement-then-reward sequence. For ADHD brains where extrinsic motivation is unreliable, this mechanism is particularly significant: connecting a task to an explicit, visceral external value can activate the motivation system that extrinsic rewards fail to reach.

---
