FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Phase 3 - Compartmentalized Focus to Beat Distraction.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-10-20T09:33:00Z
last_reviewed: "null"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:29+00:00
status: "null"
tags: ["deep_work", "focus", "project/personal/prodos", "topic/productivity"]
title: Phase 3 - Compartmentalized Focus to Beat Distraction
type: "null"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Following [[Phase 2 - Aggressive Initiation to Overcome Paralysis]], the final phase of the [[MOC - Three-Phase Protocol for Execution]] is to establish a routine of ruthless, compartmentalized focus. This is designed to beat distraction and overwhelm during the execution of the work.

1. Isolate and Eliminate Distraction: Create a "deep work" environment by turning off all notifications and removing potential interruptions. This aligns with the concept of using specific contexts like `@DeepWork` as defined in [[09 - Todoist for Task Execution]].
2. Identify and Leverage High-Value Tasks: Focus only on Key Result Areas (KRAs) or Income Generating Tasks (IGTs) during peak energy windows. This is a direct implementation of the [[MOC - ProdOS]] "Compass Over Clock" principle.
---
