type: "permanent"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Blub studies refers to the deep dive into the inner workings of everyday, mundane software tools and systems that programmers use, like programming languages, frameworks, databases, and version control systems.

This concept challenges the common assumption that learning exotic technologies is more valuable than mastering familiar ones. Instead of pursuing novelty, blub studies advocates for developing deep expertise in the tools you already use daily.

