FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Systems Generate Internal Logic in Isolation.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-10-20T10:11:00Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:26+00:00
status: ""
tags: ["culture", "emergence", "self-organization", "topic/systems"]
title: Systems Generate Internal Logic in Isolation
type: ""
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

When a system is [[Systems are Blind to Their Broader Context|blind to external context]], it cannot import its logic or values from the outside. It is therefore forced to generate its own self-referential framework of rules, logic, and meaning.

This internal "operating system" is created out of its own components and history, allowing it to function and self-regulate in isolation. This process of Self-Organisation gives rise to [[Emergence|emergent]] properties like unique cultures, behaviors, and priorities that are specific to the system itself, often governed by internal Feedback Loops.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Resilience is the Ability to Bounce Back from Setbacks.md
---
aliases: ["Bouncing Back"]
created: 2025-11-01T21:26:00Z
last_reviewed: "2025-11-01"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:28+00:00
status: "evergreen"
tags: ["character-strength", "growth", "resilience", "TheHuman/Psychology", "virtue"]
title: Resilience is the Ability to Bounce Back from Setbacks
type: "concept"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Resilience is the psychological capacity to adapt to and recover from stress, adversity, trauma, or disappointment.

It is often described as the ability to "bounce back" after a difficult experience. Resilience is not about avoiding hardship, but about navigating through it and emerging without lasting negative effects.

---
