FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Hyperfocus is a State of Intense Interest-Driven Focus in ADHD.md
---
aliases: ["ADHD Hyperfocus", "Entering the Zone"]
created: 2025-07-16T17:30:01Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:32+00:00
status: ""
tags: ["focus", "interest", "TheHuman/Health/ADHD", "TheHuman/Motivation", "topic/productivity/hyperfocus"]
title: Hyperfocus is a State of Intense Interest-Driven Focus in ADHD
type: "permanent"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Hyperfocus is a phenomenon experienced by individuals with ADHD where they can enter a state of intense, sustained concentration on a task that genuinely interests or intrigues them. During hyperfocus, typical ADHD impairments such as distractibility can seem to vanish, and executive functions related to the task can soar.

This state is a direct result of the [[The Interest-Based Nervous System in ADHD]] being fueled by a high level of intrinsic motivation, which generates a surge of dopamine. It demonstrates that the challenge in ADHD is not a lack of attention, but a dysregulation in the _direction_ and _sustainment_ of attention.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Influence of Programming Paradigms on Mental Models.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-05-26T20:32:11Z
last_reviewed: ""
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:32+00:00
status: ""
tags: []
title: Influence of Programming Paradigms on Mental Models
type: ""
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Programming paradigms (e.g., Object-Oriented Programming, Functional Programming, Procedural Programming) are not merely collections of language features; they represent fundamental approaches to thinking about and structuring solutions to problems. As such, they profoundly influence the kinds of mental models developers construct.

- Procedural Programming: Encourages a mental model based on a sequence of operations or procedures acting on data. The focus is on the "how" of computation.
- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): Promotes mental models centered around "objects" that encapsulate state (attributes) and behavior (methods). Developers think in terms of interacting entities, often modeling real-world concepts. Principles like encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism shape these models, emphasizing modularity and abstraction.
---
