FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/The 'Dopamine Shot' vs 'Relief from Anxiety' in Task Completion.md
---
aliases: ["ADHD Reward Experience"]
created: 2025-07-16T17:30:01Z
last_reviewed: "null"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:26+00:00
status: "null"
tags: ["dopamine", "neurotypical", "reward-system", "TheHuman/Health/ADHD", "TheHuman/Motivation"]
title: "The 'Dopamine Shot' vs 'Relief from Anxiety' in Task Completion"
type: "permanent"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

A critical distinction in motivational processing between ADHD and neurotypical brains lies in the subjective experience of completing a task.

- Neurotypical Experience: Completing a task, even an unenjoyable one, often results in a "little shot of dopamine." This creates a genuine feeling of pleasure or satisfaction, intrinsically reinforcing the behavior of "getting things done." This is a core feature of [[Neurotypical motivation is primarily importance-driven]].
- ADHD Experience: Completing an unpleasurable task typically brings only "relief from the anxiety" associated with it. There is often no feeling of pleasure or pride, and the struggle involved can negate any sense of accomplishment. The primary "reward" is the cessation of discomfort.
---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Instrumentalism vs Realism in Understanding.md
---
aliases: []
created: 2025-08-29T15:16:19Z
last_reviewed: "null"
modified: 2026-04-10T18:52:01+00:00
status: "null"
tags: ["philosophy-of-science", "TheHuman/Cognition/mental-model"]
title: Instrumentalism vs Realism in Understanding
type: "null"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

This distinction from the philosophy of science describes two views on theories and models:

- Instrumentalism: Views a theory as merely a tool or instrument for making accurate predictions. Its value is purely functional; it does not claim to describe reality.
- Realism: Believes a theory aims to be a true description of the underlying reality. The goal is to understand the actual mechanics of a system.
---
