FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Automated Optimization Loops Degrade Beyond 15 Iterations.md
---
created: 2026-04-10T00:00:00+00:00
modified: 2026-04-10T16:52:03+00:00
tags: [iterations, optimization, quality-control, token-management]
title: Automated Optimization Loops Degrade Beyond 15 Iterations
---
CONTENT_START:

## Automated Optimization Loops Degrade Beyond 15 Iterations

Effective automated optimization typically requires 5 to 10 iterations to converge on a quality result. Exceeding 15 iterations tends to degrade output quality and increase token costs without commensurate gain. The degradation likely reflects accumulated context drift—each iteration adds noise to the running context, and later passes optimize against a distorted signal rather than the original objective.

---
FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/PKM Generates Unique Insights via Personal Context That AI Cannot Replicate.md
---
created: 2026-04-10T00:00:00+00:00
modified: 2026-04-10T16:52:03+00:00
tags: [ai, insight, knowledge-graphs, pkm]
title: PKM Generates Unique Insights via Personal Context That AI Cannot Replicate
---
CONTENT_START:

## PKM Generates Unique Insights via Personal Context That AI Cannot Replicate

Personal Knowledge Management generates unique insights by linking ideas within an individual's personal context—their lived experience, prior knowledge, and unique trains of thought. This context is inaccessible to AI, which operates on distributional statistics across a general corpus and cannot access the subjective history that gives a specific connection its significance. Manual linking between ideas in a PKM system therefore produces insight that is genuinely non-deducible by any system without access to that personal context.

---
