FILE: /Volumes/DAL/Zettelkasten/LLMeon/30_Library/100_zettelkasten/Topology (Definition).md
---
aliases: ["Topology"]
created: 2025-11-01T11:22:13Z
last_reviewed: "2025-11-01"
modified: 2026-02-01T15:08:24+00:00
status: "seedling"
tags: ["fields", "topic/maths"]
title: Topology (Definition)
type: "definition"
updated: 
---
CONTENT_START:

Definition: Topology is the branch of mathematics that studies properties of spaces that are preserved under continuous deformations—such as stretching, bending, and twisting—but not tearing or gluing.

Abstraction from Geometry: Topology abstracts away the notion of fixed distance from geometry, focusing instead on properties like connectedness, compactness, and continuity that remain invariant under smooth transformations.

