## 1. Definitive Statement

> [!definition] Definition
> The Social Friction Coefficient is a conceptual model that represents the amount of energy and effort wasted on navigating dysfunctional social dynamics within a team or organization. A high coefficient signifies that a large portion of the team's effort is spent on Meta-Work rather than productive, essential work.
