---
---

## 3. The Four Elements (The Pillars)

### A. DJing (The Foundation)

The heartbeat of the culture.

- The Father: DJ Kool Herc. On Aug 11, 1973 (1520 Sedgwick Ave), he pioneered the "Merry-Go-Round" technique: isolating and looping the percussive "Break" of funk records to extend the danceable moment.
CONTENT_START:

> Hip Hop is a cultural movement that emerged in the 1970s South Bronx as a creative response to systemic neglect and urban decay. It is defined by Four Core Elements: "DJing (Aural), MCing (Oral), B-Boying/Breaking (Physical), and Graffiti (Visual)."

## 2. The Cultural Crucible: The Burning Bronx (1970s)

