## 1. Definitive Statement

> [!definition] Definition
> Transactional Analysis (TA) is a model that views social interactions as "transactions" between three distinct ego states: Parent, Adult, and Child. In a professional context, friction and confrontation arise from dysfunctional Parent-Child transactions. The solution is to consciously force interactions into an Adult-to-Adult framework, which is rational, objective, and data-driven.
