## 2. Historical Evolution

The genre emerged not as a prediction, but as a reaction to the anxieties of the late 20th century.

### 2.1 Origins (Post-WWII - 1970s)

- Anxiety: Post-war fears of mechanization and the Cold War.
CONTENT_START:

## 1. Definitive Statement

> [!definition] Cyberpunk
> A science-fiction sub-genre defined by the core duality of "High-Tech, Low-Life." It envisions a future of rampant technological advancement (AI, cybernetics, hyper-connectivity) juxtaposed with societal decay, corporate authoritarianism, and extreme marginalization.
